Host-side changes for the Ambilight plugin (2026-11-22), on top of the previous
patched build (see openrgb-patched-full.patch for everything vs f89cdac).

* PluginManager: a plugin seen for the first time inherited the "enabled"
  flag of the last plugin listed in OpenRGB.json (here the disabled Effects
  plugin), so it was registered disabled. Only the matching entry counts now.
* Single instance: the instance that detected the devices answers to the
  named event Local\OpenRGB_ShowWindow; a later plain launch (elevated or
  not -- OpenRGB.exe is marked Run as administrator here) signals it and
  exits, so its window comes forward instead of a client copy opening.
* ResourceManager: a rescan requested while the previous detection is still
  finishing (e.g. after Stop detection) is ignored instead of announcing a
  new detection, re-delivering the old controller list and then deleting it.
* RGBController: the update-callback list is only changed under UpdateMutex,
  the lock SignalUpdate() walks it under from SDK/plugin threads.

